Upstream's own COPYING file is the text of GPL version 2. The per-file headers
in this directory grant "version 2 of the License, or (at your option) any
later version", so this material is **GPL-2.0-or-later**. That is why LakeShark
as a whole can be, and is, distributed under GPL-3.0: GPL-2.0-or-later permits
relicensing the combined work to GPLv3. A GPL-2.0-**only** dependency would not
permit that, so if a file here is ever replaced from a fork that dropped the
"or later" wording, the root licence has to be revisited.

The full GPLv3 text is in the repository root `LICENSE`. GPLv2 is not bundled
separately because nothing here is GPL-2.0-only; if that changes, add it.

Per-file provenance, and which files this project modified, is recorded in
`UPSTREAM.md` beside this file. Modified upstream files carry a "Notice of
change" comment as GPL-2.0-or-later section 2(a) requires.

Source-code obligation
----------------------

Distributing firmware built from this directory triggers the GPL's source
obligation for the whole combined work, not only for these files. The
corresponding source has to be the actual modified sources these binaries were
built from — see `docs/THIRD_PARTY_REVIEW.md` for the export closure.
